WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.960
around the world. In the U.S., we saw 67% growth, where we gained widespread adoption.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:13.360
We have a leading share now, NBRX share of 47%. 7,000 HCPs now prescribing, and that provides us

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.200
a very strong base of physicians, which we can leverage as we move to the early breast cancer

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:24.520
launch. Similarly, outside of the U.S., 35% growth at the preferred CDK4-6 inhibitor. We

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:31.180
have a leading share of 38%. We're the fastest growing CDK4-6 inhibitor in Europe. And when you

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:36.120
look at the early breast cancer setting, we're on track now for a launch in HAP2. We've completed

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:42.320
the manufacturing adjustments in close collaboration with FDA, which we outlined earlier

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:48.700
in the year. We're now anticipating a U.S. approval by the end of quarter three. We remain confident

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:53.280
in a broad label based on the consistency of results that we've seen across the Natalie

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.080
population.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:59.680
And as we announced this morning, we have now updated Natalie data with a median follow-up

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:05.220
of four years. All patients have now completed their three-year course of the medicine. And we

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:10.480
see continued clinically meaningful benefit, consistent safety profile. We believe very

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.740
compelling results that will really support the launch of this medicine. And so we're really

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:20.780
excited to present that data at an upcoming medical meeting and continue to support that

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.480
Cascalia will hopefully be the preferred medicine for patients.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:55.290
Now, moving to slide 10. So, Plavicto demonstrated very steady growth versus prior year. Now, when you take a step back on Plavicto, we're now in a transition point where our early rapid uptake is now transitioning to a place where we need to generate demand in the next wave of centers and then eventually out in community oncology, both for the success of Plavicto, but also for the long-term success of RLT. That said, we remain highly confident in the long-term prospects of Plavicto. And we're very excited to be able to have this

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:55.770
study.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:02:01.270
to be a multibillion-dollar medicine across the various segments that it will compete in.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:05.710
We do believe that once we're through this period, we will get back to robust growth,

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:13.410
particularly driven by the PSMA-4 indication and later the HSPC and oligometastatic indications.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.910
We had growth, as I mentioned, of 44% on the quarter.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:22.610
Now, when you look specifically at the vision population, we estimate our market share is

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:28.470
in the mid-30% with 50% share in established RLT treatment sites.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:33.590
We see a dynamic where the sites where we're well-established, we could have market shares

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:34.810
above 90%.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:40.050
We have another group of sites where we're working to go from 50% to 90%.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:45.070
And then we have about a third of sites of the 475 treatment sites that we're operating

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:50.150
in, where we need to now get from 10% of share of the vision population, hopefully

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.470
up over time now to 50%, 90%.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:52.590
And that's where we're at.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:52.610
And that's where we're at.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:59.210
And that will drive the steady growth that we expect over the course of the coming quarters.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:04.750
Now, when you look specifically at what we're doing to supercharge PluVicto and also enable

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:09.970
us to build a broad capacity for the system to take on RLT, we're increasing our U.S.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:13.770
promotional efforts, including a field course expansion, which is now completed.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.190
We'll be launching a DTC campaign in quarter three.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:22.150
We'll also have the phased launch of the patient-ready dose, which is a very important

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:23.170
step.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:29.790
And then it reduces the time from providing PluVicto from around an hour to less than

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:30.390
10 minutes.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:35.570
And this will allow sites to hopefully take on more patients, especially sites that have

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:38.450
significant capacity to take on more vision patients.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:43.610
And then lastly, we have German pricing approved, which is why you've seen the uplift in the

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:47.030
XUS market, XUS sales profile.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:52.130
So looking ahead, FDA submission for PSMA4 on track in half two.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:56.930
We already have profiled the positive trend in OS and PSMA4.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.270
China submission is planned in the second half of this year.

